      "narrative": null,
      "content": "NONABELIAN MULTIPLICATIVE INTEGRATION ON SURFACES\nAMNON YEKUTIELI\nAbstract. We construct a 2-dimensional twisted nonabelian multiplicative integral.\nThis is done in the context of a Lie crossed module (an object composed of two Lie\ngroups interacting), and a pointed manifold. The integrand is a connection-curvature\npair, that consists of a Lie algebra valued 1-form and a Lie algebra valued 2-form,\nsatisfying a certain differential equation. The geometric cycle of the integration\nis a kite in the pointed manifold. A kite is made up of a 2-dimensional simplex\nin the manifold, together with a pat",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/arxiv-1007.1250v4/blocks/thm-sec-front-matter-01",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-sci:Theorem",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "theorem",
      "title": "",
      "pageStart": 1,
      "pageEnd": 3,
      "target": "thm-sec-front-matter-01.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Our main result is the 3-dimensional nonabelian Stokes Theorem. This is a totally new result. The methods we use are: the CBH Theorem for the nonabelian exponential map; piecewise smooth geometry of polyhedra; and some basic algebraic topol- ogy. The motivation for this work comes from twisted deformation quantization and descent for nonabelian gerbes. Similar questions arise in nonabelian gauge theory. Contents 0. Introduction 1. Polyhedra and Piecewise Smooth Geometry 2. Estimates for the Nonabelian Exponential Map 3. Multiplicative Integration in Dimension One 4. Multiplicative Integration",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": null
    },
